sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-29> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In organisms with a multiscale competency architecture, whose modules actively correct toward a target morphology, mutations that would be detrimental in hardwired organisms (e.g. displacing the eye) become neutral, so the architecture shields some of mutations' negative effects from selection and smooths the fitness landscape.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Multiscale competency shields mutations from selection and smooths fitness landscapes";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Evolutionary Aspects › Multi-Scale Autonomy Potentiates the Speed of Evolution”. Scope: Evolving multicellular organisms; computational models of evolution with competent cells"
}
